  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildlife Conservation Society/Government of Malaysia supporting implementation of the National Elephant Conservation Action Plan for Peninsular Malaysia - Year 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to stimulate progress on the Government of Malaysias National Elephant Conservation Action Plan (NECAP), which has a 100-year vision to maintain wild Asian elephants in the seven Malaysia states where they are extant. Specific project activities will include: 1) review land-use and produce a land-use map within three Managed Elephant Ranges (MERs) listed in the NECAP using remote sensing imagery, ground-truthed data, revised MER boundaries, and landscape elements; 2) identify areas of MERs where elephants may be present and where land-use does not provide protection; and 3) work with and meet with Federal and State government agencies to inform them about the NECAP and MERs. This project aims to have the Government of Malaysia use their resources to implement the NECAP within ten years.</narrative>
  </description>
